From 1000000000000000000000000000000000000476 Tue Sep  1 00:00:00 2026
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pstore: distinguish Gemini CPU9 progress lane refusal

The one-shot reader-mapping successor reproduced progress stage 1 with
-EBADMSG before any CPU9 request. The cpu9_progress_owner_begin() helper
uses that result for two failures. One means no CRC-valid CPU8 proof copy.
The other means the progress lane has a malformed header. Recovery
cannot distinguish them
because Gemian observes the lanes only after the fixed watchdog reboot.

Return -EUCLEAN for only the malformed progress-lane header. Preserve
-EALREADY for a committed lane. Keep every CPU8-proof result unchanged.
Extend the focused test to prove corrupt CPU8 copies still return -EBADMSG.
This adds
no read, retained write, CPU request, CPU_OFF, retry, or recovery action.
---
 fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger.c      |  2 +-
 fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger_test.c | 10 +++++++++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger.c b/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger.c
--- a/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger.c
@@ -69,6 +69,6 @@ int cpu9_progress_owner_begin(
 		       progress_ops->read(progress_context, 2) ==
 				GEMINI_TRANSITION_LEDGER_PAYLOAD_BYTES ?
-			-EALREADY : -EBADMSG;
+			-EALREADY : -EUCLEAN;
 	ret = gemini_transition_ledger_owner_begin(
 		&owner->ledger, progress_ops, progress_context, cpu8_attempt_id);
 	if (ret)
diff --git a/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger_test.c b/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger_test.c
--- a/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger_test.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/gemini_cpu9_progress_ledger_test.c
@@ -132,6 +132,14 @@ static void cpu9_progress_cpu8_gate_test(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, cpu9_progress_owner_begin(
 		&owner, &cpu9_progress_test_ops, &cpu8,
 		&cpu9_progress_test_ops, &progress, 2), -EACCES);
+	memset(&owner, 0, sizeof(owner));
+	cpu8.words[GEMINI_TRANSITION_LEDGER_HEADER_WORDS] ^= 1;
+	cpu8.words[GEMINI_TRANSITION_LEDGER_HEADER_WORDS +
+		   GEMINI_TRANSITION_LEDGER_COPY_WORDS] ^= 1;
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, cpu9_progress_owner_begin(
+		&owner, &cpu9_progress_test_ops, &cpu8,
+		&cpu9_progress_test_ops, &progress, 1), -EBADMSG);
+
 	memset(&owner, 0, sizeof(owner));
 	cpu8.words[0] = 0;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, cpu9_progress_owner_begin(
@@ -150,7 +158,7 @@ static void cpu9_progress_lane_refusal_test(struct kunit *test)
 	memset(&progress, 0xff, sizeof(progress));
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, cpu9_progress_owner_begin(
 		&owner, &cpu9_progress_test_ops, &cpu8,
-		&cpu9_progress_test_ops, &progress, 1), -EBADMSG);
+		&cpu9_progress_test_ops, &progress, 1), -EUCLEAN);
 	memset(&owner, 0, sizeof(owner));
 	cpu9_progress_test_empty(&progress);
 	progress.words[1] = GEMINI_TRANSITION_LEDGER_PAYLOAD_BYTES;
